# Line endings ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A fresh clone has to produce the same bytes on every machine.  The test suite
# loads real game files and compares decoded values, and the icon generator
# writes a binary container byte by byte — implicit, platform-dependent
# rewriting is the kind of thing that turns into "works on my machine".
#
# So: normalise to LF *in the repository*, and convert on checkout only where
# a consumer actually needs it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe reads these.  An LF-only .bat can mis-parse its own `goto` targets,
# and this one is full of them.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diff, never convert.  Git detects most of these on its own;
# "most" is not worth a mangled screenshot in the history.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.ndfbin binary
*.dic binary

# Text, stated explicitly so a later edit to the rules above cannot silently
# re-decide for the file types that matter most.
*.py text
*.md text
*.json text
*.txt text
*.spec text
*.bat text
